WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:18.010
Posed by Pierre de Fermat to Evangelista Torricelli, X thirteen is the First Isogonic Center, or Fermat Point: erect outward equilateral triangles on sides B C, C A, and A B, join their outer apexes to the opposite vertices A, B, and C, and those three segments of equal length concur at X thirteen.

2
00:00:18.430 --> 00:00:31.645
At X thirteen, each side of triangle A B C subtends an equal angle of one hundred twenty degrees, minimizing the sum of distances P A plus P B plus P C whenever every angle of A B C is less than one hundred twenty degrees.

3
00:00:31.645 --> 00:00:39.800
Its trilinear coordinates are cosecant of A plus pi over three, to cosecant of B plus pi over three, to cosecant of C plus pi over three.

4
00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:53.860
X thirteen is the isogonal conjugate of the First Isodynamic Point X fifteen, the orthocentroidal-circle inverse of the Second Isogonic Center X fourteen, and collinear with X three and the First Napoleon Point X seventeen.
